{
	"FileVersion": 3,
	"Version": 1,
	"VersionName": "0.1",
	"FriendlyName": "GSTN Presentation",
	"Description": "Presentation events (Presentation.Event.*: jump, land, run start, skid, hit, bounces, shield...) derived from the synchronized state on every machine, deduplicated per (event, frame) so a resimulation never plays an effect twice, and a per-kit/per-skin table that maps each event to a Niagara system, a sound, a camera shake and a short additive, scaled by the event's magnitude. Blueprint events for every type (online: they fire on clients too). Presentation only: nothing here is read by a simulation. No GAS, Network Prediction or Mover.",
	"Category": "Gameplay",
	"CreatedBy": "xJusteen47",
